## Purpose

Separate the exact common-source identification from a genuine lattice-spacing scaling limit, and remove pointwise convergence as an input in the exact single-scale route.

## Added

- a fixed-scale Wilson Hamiltonian transfer-orbit package;
- continuum connected correlation defined to be the same fixed finite Wilson connected correlation;
- theorem-generated pointwise convergence by `Tendsto` of a constant sequence;
- automatic conversion to the constructed transfer-orbit route;
- inherited finite exact-gap decay, continuum exact-gap bounds, and continuum clustering;
- simultaneous continuum reflection positivity, Euclidean invariance, clustering, and regularity;
- OS/Wightman readiness for explicit, Standard-Borel, compact-tightness, and countable-skeleton routes;
- equality of all four route measures with the explicit `globalObserve` pushforward law;
- core and assembly compile smoke gates.

## Boundary

This theorem applies only to the exact single-source/fixed-scale identification. It does **not** prove nontrivial ultraviolet or infinite-volume convergence as the lattice spacing tends to zero or the volume tends to infinity. Those physical scaling-limit convergence estimates, the uniform Hamiltonian spectral lower bound, connected-correlation realization, uniform initial amplitude bound, regularity estimates, and continuum gauge/symmetry data remain open analytic inputs for an unconditional four-dimensional Yang–Mills construction.
